cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use pyBELLA, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "pyBELLA"
abstract: >-
  pyBELLA is a compressible atmospheric flow solver with blended dynamics,
  switching between compressible, pseudo-incompressible, hydrostatic, lake and
  shallow-water regimes, together with an ensemble data-assimilation layer
  (ETPF, LETKF and a NEDAS interface). Geometries range from uniform Cartesian
  grids through terrain-following coordinates to the full pole-to-pole sphere.
  It is written in Python with numba kernels and an optional JAX backend.
authors:
  - given-names: Ray
    family-names: Chew
  - given-names: Tommaso
    family-names: Benacchio
  - given-names: Rupert
    family-names: Klein
version: 0.6.0
date-released: 2026-09-27
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/ray-chew/pyBELLA"
url: "https://github.com/ray-chew/pyBELLA"
keywords:
  - atmospheric dynamics
  - numerical weather prediction
  - blended soundproof-compressible model
  - pseudo-incompressible
  - data assimilation
  - terrain-following coordinates
  - JAX
